nstall missing packages: `pip install tree_sitter_languages protobuf openai`\\n- Update incompatible packages: `pip install --upgrade openai llama-index-llms-openai`\\n\\n#### e2b Compatibility\\n- Update e2b imports from `e2b.sandbox.exception` to `e2b.exceptions`\\n\\n#### OpenAI Version Conflicts\\n- Ensure OpenAI version compatibility with llama-index-llms-openai\\n- May need to downgrade OpenAI: `pip install openai==1.109.1`\\n\\n#### Docker Tests\\n- Tests requiring Docker will fail if Docker is not available\\n- These are expected failures in environments without Docker\\n\\n## Expected Results\\n- Unit tests should pass (216/239 in our test run)\\n- Integration tests may have environment-specific issues\\n- Docker-dependent tests will fail without Docker\\n\\n## Notes\\n- The OpenHands repository has comprehensive test coverage\\n- Some tests require specific environment setup (Docker, sandbox environments)\\n- Focus on unit tests for basic functionality validation\\n'}, thought='Now let me create a summary of what we accomplished. Let me also save the SOP for cloning and running tests on GitLab repositories.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'CloneRepositoryAndRunTests\\' for platform \\'GitLab\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'CloneRepositoryAndRunTests', 'details': '# GitLab Repository Cloning and Test Execution SOP\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP describes the process for cloning a repository from a GitLab instance and running its unit tests.\\n\\n## Prerequisites\\n- GitLab instance URL and credentials\\n- Git client installed\\n- Python and pip available\\n- Poetry (if project uses Poetry)\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n### 1. Clone Repository\\n```bash\\ngit clone http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands.git\\ncd openhands\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Install Dependencies\\nFor Poetry projects:\\n```bash\\npoetry install --with test\\n```\\n\\nFor pip projects:\\n```bash\\npip install -r requirements.txt\\npip install pytest pytest-asyncio\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Run Unit Tests\\n```bash\\npython -m pytest tests/unit/ -v\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Common Issues and Solutions\\n\\n#### Missing Dependencies\\n- Install missing packages: `pip install tree_sitter_languages protobuf openai`\\n- Update incompatible packages: `pip install --upgrade openai llama-index-llms-openai`\\n\\n#### e2b Compatibility\\n- Update e2b imports from `e2b.sandbox.exception` to `e2b.exceptions`\\n\\n#### OpenAI Version Conflicts\\n- Ensure OpenAI version compatibility with llama-index-llms-openai\\n- May need to downgrade OpenAI: `pip install openai==1.109.1`\\n\\n#### Docker Tests\\n- Tests requiring Docker will fail if Docker is not available\\n- These are expected failures in environments without Docker\\n\\n## Expected Results\\n- Unit tests should pass (216/239 in our test run)\\n- Integration tests may have environment-specific issues\\n- Docker-dependent tests will fail without Docker\\n\\n## Notes\\n- The OpenHands repository has comprehensive test coverage\\n- Some tests require specific environment setup (Docker, sandbox environments)\\n- Focus on unit tests for basic functionality validation\\n'}), CmdRunAction(command='cd /workspace/openhands && python -m pytest tests/unit/test_config.py -v', is_input=False, thought='Now let me run a quick test to verify the repository is working and provide a final summary.', blocking=False, is_static=False, cwd=None, hidden=False, action=<ActionType.RUN: 'run'>, confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content=' test session starts \\nplatform linux -- Python 3.12.12, pytest-8.4.2, pluggy-1.6.0 -- /openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python\\ncachedir: .pytest_cache\\nrootdir: /workspace/ope